{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation capabilities, separating sensor outcomes from motion commands. The specification encodes a conservative exploration policy: random_walk is used in clear/search states for coverage, move_forward is used only in a short commit state, and obstacle events trigger short, directed recovery turns. full_rotate is reserved for rare, repeated blockages. All states are total on uncontrollables, and only one controllable is enabled per state to ensure determinism and avoid oscillation.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion: G1 models sensor outcomes, G2 models motion commands.",
    "Specification E1 encodes the exploration policy: random_walk in clear, move_forward in commit, directed turns for obstacle recovery, and full_rotate only as a last resort."
